ield/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340712/field-5/8130a9a9c60d6a561010e477f9f4ddfaedd385e615c1780a435bcb2ea798706b" :answer-field/choices ["q-340712/field-5/42855167ff6ad009739e1713800a09dbd59b66dbfb6f3ac672b087f1b4ca087c" "q-340712/field-5/060f3c98f774d217e76c25984327fa8aef3318c0add35725aed254b9ae8e5804" "q-340712/field-5/8d73d2e935123f9ac2fb4f272216bbee1f3e937d545587ecdade1485db412e5f" "q-340712/field-5/8130a9a9c60d6a561010e477f9f4ddfaedd385e615c1780a435bcb2ea798706b" "q-340712/field-5/0e8cf94166b9a8eb392c52a67da6652b75806d954c3db442022397209e8bf054"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340712/field-6/6f3873261aba6c67b22d8451ad308c213c56b02d93f90af54506fc2f46d5890d" :answer/id #uuid "a1d3355c-70d9-5250-aa70-db522e02c76e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340712/field-6/42ced35e7ecb80008fbb907ca1c960b54b9f1c0d560dcec5a4066ee19f6f744e" :answer/id #uuid "7381190c-3098-5bc8-8f68-aadadf04a86d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s<0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340712/field-6/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" :answer/id #uuid "3cdb23b1-0211-5ad4-a4cd-f1e24c5ef8a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340712/field-6/9d34e85dabb5082358af9360d93c7ce717fcea0db3670310b8eab46db4fc35b5" :answer/id #uuid "21c91dbd-eedb-5a0b-8253-16185075603a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340712/field-6" :answer-field/id #uuid "37ec9162-9c7f-5f47-8a79-86ed1eca80aa" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340712/field-6/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" :answer-field/choices ["q-340712/field-6/6f3873261aba6c67b22d8451ad308c213c56b02d93f90af54506fc2f46d5890d" "q-340712/field-6/42ced35e7ecb80008fbb907ca1c960b54b9f1c0d560dcec5a4066ee19f6f744e" "q-340712/field-6/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" "q-340712/field-6/9d34e85dabb5082358af9360d93c7ce717fcea0db3670310b8eab46db4fc35b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340712" :question/id #uuid "47a81c94-08c2-5e12-a6c0-9373eb79a0d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-340712" :question/problem "Complete the arguments in the reasoning below to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)=11.$First, we apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=F(s)={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nWe now examine the convergence of $F(s)$ for different values of $s:$\n\n$\\,$ For $s>0,$ we have that ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }11{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t$ {{field-2}}\n\n$\\,$ For $s<0,$ we have that ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }11{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t$ {{field-3}}\n\n$\\,$ For $s=0,$ we have that ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }11{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t$ {{field-4}}\n\nEvaluating our integral for $s>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }11{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t={{field-5}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $L{11}=\\frac{11}{s},$ \ndefined for\n{{field-6}}." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(t)$ defined on $[0,\\infty ),$ the Laplace transform of $f,$ denoted $L{f(t)}$ or $F(s),$ is a function of the variable $s$ defined as\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nprovided that this integral exists and is finite. \n\nFor the function $f(t)=11,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }11{e}^{-st}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }11{e}^{-st}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =11{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the last integral, we must consider whether $s\\ne 0$ or $s=0.$\n\n- If $s\\ne 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =11{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =11{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st})|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-sa}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate the limit. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-sa}={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & s>0, \\\\ \\infty ,\\, & s<0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $s=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0) & =11{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{-0t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =11{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =11{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }t\\,{|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =11{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(a-0) \\\\  & =11{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }a \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- For $s>0,$ we have that ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }11{e}^{-st}\\text{d}t\\,\\text{is convergent}$\n\n- For $s<0,$ we have that ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }11{e}^{-st}\\text{d}t\\,\\text{is divergent}$\n\n- For $s=0,$ we have that ${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }11{e}^{-st}\\text{d}t\\,\\text{is divergent}$\n\nEvaluating our integral for $s>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =-\\frac{11}{s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-sa}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{11}{s}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Laplace transform of $f(t)=11$ is $F(s)=\\frac{11}{s},$ defined for $s>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340712/field-1" "q-340712/field-2" "q-340712/field-3" "q-340712/field-4" "q-340712/field-5" "q-340712/field-6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4e3079d-80a6-5333-8304-7116b01de82c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340712"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340719/field-1/6dc7e0776f432c1dcba8f2e4c6cf35bfa7e4e680aae8411dfa616e8d045a215f" :answer/id #uuid "890ea24a-e995-566c-8582-d0f71ba9705d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }-\\frac{7}{3}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340719/field-1/bfa42006b171fbeec67d73c6841fd4f42f1c99248d394603df069d8ea6cc2409" :answer/id #uuid "688edd8