/math :answer/value "s\\ge 7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340724/field-5/9d34e85dabb5082358af9360d93c7ce717fcea0db3670310b8eab46db4fc35b5" :answer/id #uuid "0f5ff834-1852-5c79-a124-3b4623a42963" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340724/field-5" :answer-field/id #uuid "0008300e-5a24-5f3d-9df8-de8b5ae208b2" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340724/field-5/42306025e95a9f849d47e35290444dc33950dd58fc762bdea63297c1ae2da468" :answer-field/choices ["q-340724/field-5/42306025e95a9f849d47e35290444dc33950dd58fc762bdea63297c1ae2da468" "q-340724/field-5/6f3873261aba6c67b22d8451ad308c213c56b02d93f90af54506fc2f46d5890d" "q-340724/field-5/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" "q-340724/field-5/8aa9255905047a28b15883a68e2f972c4480c71f3dda7b8ed3a6196176f7a49e" "q-340724/field-5/9d34e85dabb5082358af9360d93c7ce717fcea0db3670310b8eab46db4fc35b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340724" :question/id #uuid "ec5e9fbd-5db3-5861-9fcc-0a2b2adb0caf" :question/math-academy-id "q-340724" :question/problem "Complete the arguments in the reasoning below to find the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{7t}.$First, we apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=F(s)={{field-1}}\n$$\n\nWe now examine the convergence of $F(s)$ for different values of $s:$\n\n$\\,$ For {{field-2}}\nthe integral is divergent.\n\n$\\,$ For {{field-3}}\nthe integral is convergent.\n\nEvaluating our integral in the convergent case, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(7-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t={{field-4}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $L{{e}^{7t}}=\\frac{1}{s-7},$ \ndefined for\n{{field-5}}." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(t)$ defined on $[0,\\infty ),$ the Laplace transform of $f,$ denoted $L{f(t)}$ or $F(s),$ is a function of the variable $s$ defined as\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nprovided that this integral exists and is finite. \n\nFor the function $f(t)={e}^{7t},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}\\cdot {e}^{7t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st+7t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(7-s)t}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(7-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(7-s)t}\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the last integral, we must consider whether $s\\ne 7$ or $s=7.$\n\n- If $s\\ne 7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(7-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{7-s}{e}^{(7-s)t})|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7-s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7-s)a}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7}(1-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7-s)a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7}-\\frac{1}{s-7}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7-s)a}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's evaluate the limit. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7-s)a}={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & s>7, \\\\ \\infty ,\\, & s<7.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- If $s=7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(7-7)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{0t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }t\\,{|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(a-0) \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }a \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- For $s\\le 7$ the integral is divergent.\n\n- For $s>7$ the integral is convergent.\n\nEvaluating for $s>7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =\\frac{1}{s-7}-\\frac{1}{s-7}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7-s)a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7}-\\frac{1}{s-7}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{7t}$ is $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-7},$ defined for $s>7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340724/field-1" "q-340724/field-2" "q-340724/field-3" "q-340724/field-4" "q-340724/field-5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a2fd0466-9f47-5adc-911a-f297858951b1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340724"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340731/field-1/6371ca9d8ff03d8d0452ae0e16be8d8dfdadd8ada8fe00ba234eb1c9e86c2a63" :answer/id #uuid "f2314f12-64b5-57b0-897d-e81d40884610" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340731/field-1/0431ec5b3e6e94ada994722118e38bed3b808c19c6e613aeb98a7af56ff159fe" :answer/id #uuid "86a26809-f2e8-543e-98c3-76b5b7bfa8d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340731/field-1/25e4c8e80942ada30ea45c9e9bd27e207cc72f3f06d0be6699310afb05c96405" :answer/id #uuid "44d4d2e8-c35f-5be1-be93-177db6e8ccc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340731/field-1/a2711e480497078a166c929799db8e7b7796533e5c4ddcda461b2f52fd9c14d8" :answer/id #uuid "d36b7ae2-aef2-501c-85e4-e300a2d6b6ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }{e}^{(1/4+s)t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340731/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac8beaef-0738-5c58-85d9-0a540d390e02" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-340731/field-1/25e4c8e80942ada30ea45c9e9bd27e207cc72f3f06d0be6699310afb05c96405" :answer-field/choices ["q-340731/field-1/6371ca9d8ff03d8d0452ae0e16be8d8dfdadd8ada8fe00ba234eb1c9e86c2a63" "q-340731/field-1/0431ec5b3e6e94ada994722118e38bed3b808c19c6e613aeb98a7af56ff159fe" "q-340731/field-1/25e4c8e8094